cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  BSARD Retrieval (RQ1): Sparse, Dense, Hybrid and Agentic
  Retrieval over Belgian Statutory Law
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using these
  metadata. Please also cite the underlying BSARD dataset
  (see DATA_LICENSE.md).
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Marios
    family-names: Paschalidis
    email: paschalidismarios@gmail.com
    affiliation: KU Leuven
repository-code: "https://github.com/MariusPasch/bsard-rag-thesis"
abstract: >-
  Code and experiments for a systematic comparison of
  retrieval methods (sparse BM25, dense bi-encoders, hybrid
  fusion, and agentic LLM-judge / CRAG / ReAct pipelines)
  over the Belgian Statutory Article Retrieval Dataset
  (BSARD), conducted as part of a master's thesis at
  KU Leuven.
keywords:
  - information retrieval
  - legal NLP
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - BSARD
  - dense retrieval
  - reranking
license: MIT
